  "description": "BALLIL crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 4. Reported CIF formula moiety: C192 H184 Er9 O42 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er1C (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er1B (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er1A (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3A (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3C (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3B (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.548-5.023 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.34-170.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [HNEt3][Er9(μ4-O)2(μ3-OH)8(pmc)16]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
